LinkSpec – Third-party licenses
================================

LinkSpec itself is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

Bundled data
------------
* usb.ids (http://www.linux-usb.org/usb.ids) – used under the 3-clause BSD
  License. Full text: data/LICENSE.usb-ids.

GUI toolkit
-----------
* Slint (https://slint.dev) – used under the Slint Royalty-free Desktop,
  Mobile, and Web Applications License v2.0. The app shows the required
  attribution ("Made with Slint") in the About view.

Rust crates
-----------
The release workflow generates a complete list of all Rust dependencies and
their licenses with `cargo about` (packaging/about.hbs) and ships it as
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.html next to every binary. `cargo deny check licenses`
(deny.toml) enforces the allowed license set in CI.
